{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Arise, walk through the land, its length and its breadth</b>. It is possible that this is permission, according to his desire — He said to him: wherever you wish to walk in the land, go, for I will be with you and I will guard you from the harm of the nations; \"for to you I will give it,\" that is, it shall be yours. And if it is a commandment that he should walk through all its length and breadth to take possession of his gift, as I explained (Ramban on Genesis 12:6), he was not commanded to do this immediately, and indeed he did so, for now he was in the east and afterward he went to the land of the Philistines, which is in the west, and so he fulfilled the commandment during his lifetime. And the sense of \"to you and to your seed\" is that he should take hold of the gift from now in order to bequeath it to his seed, as our Sages said (Bava Batra 119a): it is an inheritance to them from their fathers. And by way of the plain sense, it is possible that he would be ruler over it and a prince of Elohim within it, in every place that he would walk in that land:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:28:10.268759750Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}